# `cachedOf` reads a field, tests it and returns what it has read: four operations. They stand at the call; the way on which the field is empty goes to ONE ordinary block that enters `cachedOf` as the call would, and the head runs once more there: it has done nothing.
# `sizeOf` asks its parameter itself and `plainOf` asks more than four operations' worth: both stay calls. A call in tail position stays one behind the copied head.
# RUN: walk f5 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=f2
# CHECK: Branch {{*}}notTaken [[call]]()
# CHECK: [[call]]():
# CHECK: = CallDirect {{*}}function=f2 {{*}}[isNeverInlined]
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key="cached"
# RUN(REST): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# REST-NOT: function=f1
# RUN(PARAMETER): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# PARAMETER-NOT: frame 1 callee=f3
# RUN(LONG): walk f7 mechanisms=all
# LONG-NOT: frame 1 callee=f4
# RUN(TAIL): walk f8 mechanisms=all
# TAIL: frame 1 callee=f2
# TAIL: [[result]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f2
# TAIL-NEXT: ReturnCall [[result]]
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 25 25 1 1 29 10 2 4
